From 3a9f8d8b729100c547b63ae1f762e31d329d5c9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 27 Apr 2025 14:22:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plugwise: use last 2 bytes of Appliance ID as domoticz ID

In its current form, the Anna plugin assigns a non-deterministic number
to each 'device', leading to all devices getting a new, different ID
when new 'devices' are added. This can and will also happen when the
plug gets extended to add more features, e.g. adding support for the
temperature calibration field in 'Jip' sensors.
To make the ID both deterministic and repeatable, use the last 2 bytes
of their Zigbee address.

The exception to this are the 'Presets', the migration logic has too
many assumptions about everything being a one room Anna setup to fix
properly.

Another issue is that having multiple sensors of the same kind will also
lead to ID confusion.
When using this plugin with a Plugwise Adam in a multiroom configuation,
there will be more than one sensor of a specific type, for example one
'Jip' temperature/humidity sensor per room and/or one 'Floor' thermostat per
room.
Or even in a single room config, underfloor radiant heating will likely
have multiple zones, each zone can have a 'Tom' valve to regulate the
flow.

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [WIP]
---
 hardware/AnnaThermostat.cpp | 46 +++++++++++++++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hardware/AnnaThermostat.cpp b/hardware/AnnaThermostat.cpp
index 351f27c2f..6dfc8148c 100644
--- a/hardware/AnnaThermostat.cpp
+++ b/hardware/AnnaThermostat.cpp
@@ -457,6 +457,7 @@ void CAnnaThermostat::GetMeterDetails()
